nce included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says &quot;Year confirmed when you book&quot;; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car&#39;s page before its first handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), <b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The partner&#39;s monthly statement shows each rental at the sheet rate, the cut and the payout; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner&#39;s share in proportion; a discount CarmaCars gives comes out of the markup.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-s-crm-01-motors-gohighlevel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner&#39;s CRM (01 Motors&#39; GoHighLevel)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> tile, then the partner (or <b class="gd-ui">CRM link</b> on the partner&#39;s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box <b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors gives us</b> on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press <b class="gd-ui">Connect</b>. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. <b class="gd-ui">Test connection</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Run sync now</b> do it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors sees</b>: CarmaCars&#39; own cars and program owners&#39; cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a &quot;CarmaCars Vehicles&quot; object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner&#39;s. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change what we share</b> to leave out program owners&#39; cars, rates, availability or photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Partner price</b>: the site&#39;s rates, or the site&#39;s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Their cars coming in</b>: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows <b class="gd-ui">Add as their car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Leads both ways</b> (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Feed, widget and booking links</b>: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/&lt;car&gt; that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. <b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin &gt; Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-add-a-rental-by-hand" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental by hand</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>. For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Standing with the renter at pickup? Press <b class="gd-ui">Start at pickup</b>: type the renter&#39;s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press <b class="gd-ui">Hold the car and finish later</b>. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (<b class="gd-ui">Save draft</b> saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: <b class="gd-ui">Phone</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Walk-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Turo or another platform</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacement</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owner using own car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line (&quot;$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan&quot;): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter&#39;s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner&#39;s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b> once the insurer confirms it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer&#39;s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press <b class="gd-ui">Add another payment (paid in parts)</b> and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">15</span><div class="gd-t">The rental agreement: Send it to sign online, or Already signed on paper (a task asks for the scan). The calendar: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">16</span><div class="gd-t">Tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b> if they should not get the confirmation. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal, or on paper and you record it. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Verified in person</b> records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-retire-or-delete-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Retire or delete a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Retire or delete</b>, or the car&#39;s own page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Retire this car</b> takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> brings it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete this car</b> removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the same page, <b class="gd-ui">Delete all sample cars</b> deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-sample-cars-on-the-site" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample cars on the site</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site</b>. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide sample cars</b> asks first (&quot;Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?&quot;); press <b class="gd-ui">Hide them</b> to take every sample car off the site at once, or <b class="gd-ui">Keep them</b>. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show sample cars</b> puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the site each one is marked &quot;Example car&quot;. They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-why-a-car-is-not-on-the-site-yet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Why a car is not on the site yet</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the card Not on the site yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The same car is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The car comes off both once it is on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-placeholder-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Placeholder bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b> (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a placeholder</b>. Not once money was taken or the car went out. <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking</b> undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Competing for these dates</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Also on this car for these dates</b> once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-tolls-when-two-rentals-overlap" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tolls when two rentals overlap</h2><p class="gd-p">Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'chapter', 'tolls-and-tickets', 'See who is on the site right now and what they look at, with buying signals, and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers the chat first; you take over whenever you want, and it hands over by itself for complaints, damage, payments and anything it should not answer.

## Live visitors

Visitors who accepted analytics (or got the notice in Canada outside Quebec and the US), known customers on their own booking pages and anyone in a chat.

1. Open **Today** > **Live visitors**. "Live now" counts who is on the site now (seen in the last 5 minutes; an open page says it is still there every 45 seconds, so someone reading one page stays on the list). "Visitors today" counts people, with their visits below. The other tiles count hot visitors now, known customers now and chats today. The menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site.
2. Visitors who chose necessary cookies only are never recorded: a line under the tiles says how many chose that today. Closing the tab takes a visitor off the list at once.
3. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100, with Hot (60 or more), Warm (30 or more) or Cold. The list is sorted by it; choose "Most recent" in Sort, or tick "Hot and warm only".
4. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Reached step 3 of the request form · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals of the visit; the dots say how strong each is.
5. Each visitor also shows their name when known (signed in, or arrived from one of our emails), otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone"; the page and car they are on, and how many others look at that car now; the device, city, the site or campaign that sent them and "from an ad".
6. Suggested: the best next step and the message to send. Press **Invite to chat with this message** to send it at once, **Edit the message** to change it first, **Offer a 10% discount code**, **Assign to Sales** or, when their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car**.
7. Press **Pages** for every page and event of the visit with each signal''s points, or **Start a chat** to write your own message. They see it in a bubble and reply from it.
8. Below: hot visitors today (and whether someone acted), the signals of the last 24 hours, and the most viewed cars of the week with prices shown and the car most compared with each. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.

1. On their line, press **Name**. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press **Save the name**.
2. The name shows on Live visitors, the visit''s pages, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.
3. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.
4. Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours ("Booked"). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat''s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.
5. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Live map

A map of the Greater Toronto Area and around it (Kitchener and Guelph to Cobourg and Peterborough, Niagara to Barrie) with a dot for every lead, made for a TV or monitor in the office.

1. Open **Today** > **Live map**. The four numbers: who is on the site now, requests today, cars on rent now and the money collected this month.
2. Each dot is one person, coloured by their stage: green on rent or booked, amber requests and forms (a request, a form sent or a form started), cyan on the site now or a game played, grey past renters. The stages under the map count each one; press one to hide or show it. Renters on rent, bookings and hot leads show as a round photo of their car in a ring of their stage colour (the make''s initial when the car has no photo). A visitor on the site breathes slowly, a new event sends one ripple, and crowded dots join in a count (press it to zoom in). Busy areas glow softly. The C marker is home base (the delivery origin in **Settings** > **Program**), with a thin line running to each car on rent or booked.
3. Hover over or press a dot for its card: the name, the score from 0 to 100 and its strongest reasons, and the car they looked at last with its daily price. The table below lists everyone of the last 30 days and everything current; press a heading to sort, press a name for the signals, and **Show on the map**.
4. Names show as the first name and last initial, phones as their last 4 digits, and no email. Tick **Show details** to see them in full (never in TV mode).
5. Press **Open TV mode** on the computer connected to the TV and make the browser full screen (F11 on Windows, Control Command F on a Mac). The map fills the screen with the four numbers on top and the stages at its top left; along the bottom, On the road: the cars on rent and those picked up today, with the renter and when the car is due back; on the right, the hottest lead with the car''s photo (changing every 10 seconds) and the live feed, one line per event. It refreshes every 30 seconds and hides the pointer when the mouse is still.

- Where a dot goes: the approximate place of the visitor''s network (about 1 km, from Cloudflare), else the centre of the renter''s home city or of the visit''s city. Nothing is looked up and no address is shown. People with no place are counted under the map.
- The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.
- The fleet layer: once CarmaCars'' trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick **Fleet** to show or hide it.

## The signals

Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.

- Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.
- Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a "near me" search.
- Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.
- Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.
- Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.

## Hot visitors and the actions

- When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.
- A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.
- Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.
- Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago") so two people do not write to the same visitor.

## Signal settings

1. Open **Today** > **Live visitors** and press **Signal settings**.
2. Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).
3. Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for "Pickup soon", 3 searches for "Searching dates again and again"), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.
4. Press **Save the signals**. The next look at each visit uses them.

## Follow-up tasks

Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours".

- An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.
- The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.
- A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.
- A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.
- The thresholds are in **Settings** > **Program**, group "Live visitors and live chat", with how long "on the site now" lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.

## Recovery emails

Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.

- An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.
- A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).
- Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).
- They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, "Booking recovery emails".

## Interest in a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, a car, Overview: "Interest on the site" shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has "Most viewed cars this week".

## A renter''s visits

On a renter''s page (People > Renters, the name) and on a booking''s History tab, "On the site" lists when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, which cars they looked at, and their chats.

## Live chat

1. A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press **Open the chat**. Or open **Bookings** > **Live chat**. The menu counts chats waiting for a person. Open chats come first, those waiting for a person on top, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor''s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over**: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press **Send** (or Enter).
4. **Hand back to the assistant** lets it answer again. **Close** ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. **Email the transcript** sends it any time.
5. Notify me: "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" and desktop alerts in this browser. You are on shift while Live chat or Live visitors is open.

> Tip: The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car''s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor''s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose "I sourced this client" on the quote or offer.

## The assistant''s settings

In Program settings, "Live visitors and live chat": the chat on or off, the AI first or not, its model, the neurons it may use a day (6,000, about 10 chats; then chats wait for a person), the greeting on car pages after some seconds (off by default), how long chats and visits are kept, as the privacy policy says: chats 12 months, the pages of a visit 90 days, the visit''s summary in Visitor history 13 months, and the daily totals, which name no one, 3 years.

## What a visitor typed

A visitor who typed contact details into a form shows them on their line: "Typed into the booking request, not sent: Maya Chen, maya@example.com", with **Email not confirmed** until they open the link we emailed, and **Renter page**.
